A z3 error is reported, never ignored. sea-vc builds without exceptions, so z3++
cannot throw: outside input (--z3-tactic, --z3-param) is checked where it
enters, and every z3 context has an error handler (smt.z3-internal) behind it.

A tactic z3 cannot parse (z3 alone prints "(error" and carries on):
RUN: not sea-vc %S/seam/eq-audit.mlir --program=memset --lower --seam --z3-tactic='(then' 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=TACTIC
TACTIC: Error: z3 rejects --z3-tactic '(then': {{.*}} [vc.z3-tactic]
RUN: not sea-vc %S/seam/eq-audit.mlir --program=memset --lower --seam --z3-tactic=nosuchtactic 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=NAME
NAME: Error: z3 rejects --z3-tactic 'nosuchtactic': {{.*}} [vc.z3-tactic]
NAME-NOT: smt.z3-internal

A z3 parameter z3 rejects (z3 alone warns and carries on):
RUN: not sea-vc %S/seam/eq-audit.mlir --program=memset --lower --seam --z3-param=nosuchparam=1 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=PNAME
PNAME: Error: z3 rejects --z3-param nosuchparam=1: {{.*}}unknown parameter{{.*}} [smt.z3-param]
RUN: not sea-vc %S/seam/eq-audit.mlir --program=memset --lower --seam --z3-param=warning=false --z3-param=nosuchparam=1 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=PNAME
RUN: not sea-vc %S/seam/eq-audit.mlir --program=memset --lower --seam --z3-param=rlimit=abc 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=PVALUE
PVALUE: Error: z3 rejects --z3-param rlimit=abc: {{.*}} [smt.z3-param]
RUN: not sea-vc %S/seam/eq-audit.mlir --program=memset --lower --seam --z3-param=sat.euf=1 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=PBOOL
PBOOL: Error: z3 rejects --z3-param sat.euf=1: {{.*}} [smt.z3-param]
A good parameter and a good tactic still run:
RUN: sea-vc %S/seam/eq-audit.mlir --program=memset --lower --seam --z3-param=smt.random_seed=3 --z3-tactic=smtfd 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=OK
OK: result: sat

A z3 memory-out is not an internal error: it is the memory limit's outcome
(unknown, exit 3), in a check, outside one (reach: the memout is z3's error
code), and when z3 cannot even make a context. The limits sit far from z3's
baseline (a context and a solver need under 30 MB, by host): the queries of
Inputs/z3-memout.mlir need far more than the limit (@check: hundreds of MB in
the check; @sort: a 128 MB sort table when the first term is translated), and
the context case uses 1 MB.
RUN: sh -c 'sea-vc "$0" --program=check --z3-param=memory_max_size=48 >%t.plain 2>&1; test $? -eq 3' %S/Inputs/z3-memout.mlir
RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=MEMOUT < %t.plain
RUN: sh -c 'sea-vc "$0" --program=sort --reach --z3-param=memory_max_size=48 >%t.reach 2>&1; test $? -eq 3' %S/Inputs/z3-memout.mlir
RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=MEMOUT < %t.reach
RUN: sh -c 'sea-vc "$0" --program=check --z3-param=memory_max_size=1 >%t.ctx 2>&1; test $? -eq 3' %S/Inputs/z3-memout.mlir
RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=MEMOUT < %t.ctx
RUN: sh -c 'sea-vc "$0" --program=check --z3-tactic=qfbv --z3-param=memory_max_size=48 >%t.tac 2>&1; test $? -eq 3' %S/Inputs/z3-memout.mlir
RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=MEMOUT < %t.tac
RUN: sh -c 'sea-vc "$0" --program=sort --reach --z3-param=memory_max_size=48 --mem-limit=2000 >%t.lim 2>&1; test $? -eq 3' %S/Inputs/z3-memout.mlir
RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=MEMLIM < %t.lim
MEMOUT: result: unknown
MEMOUT-NOT: smt.z3-internal
MEMLIM: result: unknown
MEMLIM: mem-limit: hit
MEMLIM-NOT: smt.z3-internal

An error z3 reports from inside sea-vc reaches the handler (planted: an invalid
API call):
RUN: not sea-vc %S/seam/eq-audit.mlir --program=memset --lower --seam --z3-plant-error 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=PLANT
PLANT: Error: z3 reported an error (code {{[0-9]+}}): {{.*}} [smt.z3-internal]
PLANT-NOT: result:

